#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184911} :activity/id #uuid "4b97fda7-9c55-5323-b8d1-fded3bb4c112" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050095 :topic/id #uuid "2cec8fb8-053f-5ba0-99fb-d1ef0e4f826d" :topic/math-academy-id 3827} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184911 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186185371 :tutorial/content "Let's think about how to graph the solutions to the following two-variable inequality:\n\n$$\ny \\geq x\n$$\n\nSince this is a two-variable inequality, we must represent its solutions in the $xy$-plane.\n\nWe start by replacing the inequality symbol\n\n$$\n(\\geq)\n$$\n\nwith an equals sign $(=)$ and plot the resulting line. In this case, we get the line $y=x$.\n\n![](images/ee/ee227c66ae46e235a55af2d93cce25b2128cd8b734c74f9c0ef46fef2673c52f.png)\n\nNotice that we have a \"greater than *or equal to*\" inequality\n\n$$\n(\\geq)\n$$\n\nTherefore, we draw a *solid* line (as opposed to a dotted or dashed line). The solid line indicates that points on the line are solutions to our inequality.\n\nNow, since we're solving\n\n$$\ny \\geq x\n$$\n\nwe need to shade all points whose $y$-value is *greater than or equal to* its $x$-value. This is given by all of the points that lie *above* our solid line or *on* the line. So, let's shade these in.\n\n![](images/bf/bfa570421368fcc9de6105d9b6389aa45fcdf5124360c3cb04705acf23966526.png)\n\nAnd we're done! All of the points in the shaded region satisfy the inequality\n\n$$\ny \\geq x\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "8fcd0500-368c-549f-b5ec-21d14b014cf0" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8725 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "25e97899-836e-5a6e-92b2-5f93b021a4ef" :step/math-academy-id 139355 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184912}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184912 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186185372 :tutorial/content "When solving two-variable inequalities, it's often helpful to test and ensure that we've shaded the correct region.\n\nTo demonstrate, let's go back to the following inequality:\n\n$$\ny \\geq x\n$$\n\nThe solution to this inequality is indicated by the shaded region below.\n\n![](images/7c/7ce23c4ddfbae67f1f2439ace6c5947d741c4ffc1154fbc182b6ec205d49d32d.png)\n\nTo check that we've shaded the correct region, we pick a point inside the shaded region and verify that it satisfies the original inequality. Let's pick the point $(0,1)$.\n\n![](images/17/1786c43582a010b35fd66da75bb1540829b2a64e05f0c628863b1b6c1bdfb73f.png)\n\nWhen we substitute the coordinates $(0,1)$ into our inequality, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}y & \\ge x \\\\ 1 & \\ge 0✓\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis indicates that we have shaded the correct region." :tutorial/id #uuid "6fb8fcba-7b56-5496-8e21-925eaee7d301" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8726 :tutorial/title "Testing the Solution"} :step/id #uuid "ece63767-9280-5617-a4cd-64afbb1f5134" :step/math-academy-id 139356 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184913}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184913 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184156 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186183937 :question/id #uuid "24103b17-4722-598c-861a-4f79c6e8c8bb" :question/math-academy-id "e-14039"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "613d9e73-0adc-5f41-b15e-384979c1c4bb" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049716} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050361} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050519}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184486} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184810}] :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Solution to a “Greater Than or Equal To” Inequality"} :step/id #uuid "453c7f99-775d-5594-ad32-2bdc475c3762" :step/math-academy-id 139357 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184914}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184914 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186185374 :tutorial/content "Let's now think about how to graph the solutions to the inequality\n\n$$\ny \\leq x\n$$\n\nAs before, we start by replacing the inequality symbol\n\n$$\n(\\leq)\n$$\n\nwith an equals sign $(=)$ and plot the resulting line $y=x$.\n\n![](images/2e/2e681fdbbc42611f21bb22dde689ade7fb567dfb0ca169b46db66e448f7cc289.png)\n\nNotice that we have a \"less than *or equal to*\" inequality\n\n$$\n(\\leq)\n$$\n\nTherefore, we draw a *solid* line.\n\nNow, since we're solving\n\n$$\ny \\leq x\n$$\n\nwe need to shade all points whose $y$-value is *smaller than or equal to* its $x$-value. This is given by all of the points that lie *below* our solid line or *on* the line.\n\n![](images/63/6306a20f8570c194ff7aac3218267972f44056c24ea2dc6e6e29971784063523.png)\n\nAnd we're done! All of the points in the shaded region satisfy the inequality\n\n$$\ny \\leq x\n$$\n\nTo check that we've shaded the correct region, we pick a point inside the shaded region and check that it satisfies the original inequality. Let's pick the point $(1,0)$.\n\n![](images/e9/e9a3b18ef7f825b823dc24f01f9027f0ca7d49285fbea94c9daee38ccc4d38e9.png)\n\nWhen we substitute the coordinates $(1,0)$ into our inequality, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}y & \\le x \\\\ 0 & \\le 1✓\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis indicates that we have shaded the correct region." :tutorial/id #uuid "e1469811-00d3-50b2-be5b-ff446e585616" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8734 :tutorial/title "Solving \"Less Than or Equal To\" Inequalities"} :step/id #uuid "2beddcc0-9593-5354-8fe4-3cf0e10397f8" :step/math-academy-id 139360 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184915}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184915 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184157 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186183940 :question/id #uuid "5831f050-1664-5987-8ea9-e9f6706c7143" :question/math-academy-id "e-14049"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "19159c1b-3913-543f-bfd8-b5f43a50b802" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184479} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184481}] :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Solution to a “Less Than or Equal To” Inequality"} :step/id #uuid "db5374ba-e47d-550f-88be-a5ec37bb7bd3" :step/math-academy-id 139361 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184916}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184916 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184158 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186183942 :question/id #uuid "0e4631f7-4b32-5522-b48f-7d50c6e89c4d" :question/math-academy-id "e-14062"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "06c5075a-a4cf-5e56-8a6f-2e1636b2ee0a" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184546} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184547} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234156} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234157}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Inequality Corresponding to a Given Graph"} :step/id #uuid "12fc0ed1-a888-571b-b41a-c290bcb43e3a" :step/math-academy-id 139364}] :activity/title "Graphing Non-Strict Two-Variable Linear Inequalities" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186184412}]}
